## Traveling Collimated Beam Projector (TCBP) campaign at ZTF

During my PhD, I was involved in ZTF calibration, more precisely in the filters calibration part. That led me to take part in a two week of measurement of the Zwicky Transient Facility camera with the TCBP. The TCBP emit a parallel monochromatic light beam with a controllable wavelength, which allows simulating an infinite light source. That allows to measure the transmission of the optics of the telescope and the CCD quantum efficiency with and without the filters. These two weeks of measurements made it possible to develop a realistic model of the ZTF filters, which can be used to model the light curves of Type Ia supernovae. This entire campaign is summarized in an article currently in the works.  

## Pic du Midi Observations

During my master's program, I conducted an observational project at the Pic du Midi in the Pyrenees in France. During those two weeks, I was able to use the observatory's T50 telescope to make various observations of the sky. 
